<!--
  iOS local-network permission keys for TV Remote.

  These are NOT a standalone file — they are the keys you must MERGE into the
  real ios/Runner/Info.plist that `flutter create .` generates. iOS 14+ blocks
  all local-network traffic (our SSDP multicast + the SSAP WebSocket) until the
  user grants the permission prompt, and it fails SILENTLY if these keys are
  missing or malformed: discovery simply finds nothing.

  Paste every <key>…</key> pair below inside the top-level <dict> of Info.plist.
-->

<!-- 1. Why we need the local network (shown in the iOS permission prompt). -->
<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
<string>TV Remote needs local network access to find and control your TV on Wi-Fi.</string>

<!-- 2. Bonjour service types we browse. iOS requires every service type used
     with the local network to be declared here. SSDP itself is raw UDP, but
     declaring these is required for the permission to cover our discovery and
     is needed once we add Bonjour/mDNS-based discovery. -->
<key>NSBonjourServices</key>
<array>
  <string>_ssdp._udp</string>
  <string>_lg-smart-device._tcp</string>
  <string>_lgsmartdevice._tcp</string>
  <string>_airplay._tcp</string>
</array>

<!--
  IMPORTANT — also required for the multicast M-SEARCH send:

  Sending to 239.255.255.250:1900 needs the "Multicast Networking" capability
  (com.apple.developer.networking.multicast). Steps:
    1. Enable it for your App ID in the Apple Developer portal
       (https://developer.apple.com/account -> Identifiers -> your App ID ->
        Additional Capabilities -> Multicast Networking). This requires a
        one-time request/approval from Apple.
    2. In Xcode: Runner target -> Signing & Capabilities -> + Capability ->
       add the multicast entitlement, which writes:
         <key>com.apple.developer.networking.multicast</key><true/>
       into Runner.entitlements.

  Without the multicast entitlement, RawDatagramSocket.send() to the multicast
  group is dropped by iOS and no TVs are found — even with the keys above set.
-->
